  {
   "id": "va-20261-HB168",
   "state": "VA",
   "session": "20261",
   "session_name": "2026 Regular Session",
   "number": "HB168",
   "chamber": "House",
   "type": "bill",
   "title": "Election of certain governing bodies; conversion to single-member districts.",
   "summary": "Election of certain governing bodies; conversion to single-member districts. Requires every locality with a population of 400,000 or greater to elect the members of its governing body by individual single-member districts. The bill provides that a governing body's presiding officer may be elected at large. The bill further provides that any such governing body that does not already meet the requirements of the bill shall establish the required districts and shall reapportion the representation in the governing body in accordance with general law. Finally, the bill provides that for any such governing body that, prior to 2026, adopted an ordinance with a map to elect its members by individual single-member districts, such ordinance shall become effective upon the effective date of this act. This bill is identical to SB 51.",
